  <!-- ─── PAGE 1: ABOUT ME ─── -->
  <item>
    <title>About Me</title>
    <link>https://animeshbiswas.com/about/</link>
    <pubDate>Wed, 27 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
    <dc:creator><![CDATA[animesh]]></dc:creator>
    <guid isPermaLink="false">https://animeshbiswas.com/?page_id=2</guid>
    <description></description>
    <content:encoded><![CDATA[
<!-- wp:heading {"level":1} -->
<h1>Dr. Animesh Biswas, PhD</h1>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>Global Health Practitioner · UNFPA Bangladesh</strong></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Dr. Animesh Biswas is a global health practitioner at <em>UNFPA Bangladesh</em>, working at the difficult edges of reproductive health — where policy meets crisis, and where systems must be built before they can be measured.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>He pioneered the use of <strong>Cash and Voucher Assistance for Sexual and Reproductive Health outcomes</strong> in humanitarian emergencies — a model now studied, validated and replicated across multiple countries. The work began in the Rohingya response in Cox's Bazar and has since travelled.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>A standing member of the <strong>WHO Global MPDSR Technical Working Group</strong> for over five years, he has contributed case studies to WHO's 2024 global report and advised on the international guidance for cash-based programming in SRH.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Practice areas</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul>
  <li><strong>Maternal &amp; Perinatal Health</strong> — Evidence-based strategies to reduce maternal mortality at community and facility level.</li>
  <li><strong>MPDSR Systems</strong> — Advancing Maternal Perinatal Death Surveillance &amp; Response through the WHO Technical Working Group.</li>
  <li><strong>SRH in Emergencies</strong> — Designing and delivering reproductive health programmes for displaced and crisis-affected populations.</li>
  <li><strong>Cash &amp; Voucher for SRH</strong> — Pioneered CVA for reproductive health outcomes in humanitarian emergencies.</li>
</ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>Key facts</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul>
  <li>130+ publications and research outputs</li>
  <li>12+ years of global health practice</li>
  <li>Programme reach across 15+ countries</li>
  <li>5+ years on WHO MPDSR Technical Working Group</li>
  <li>PhD · UNFPA Bangladesh (2014–present)</li>
  <li>Based in Dhaka, Bangladesh</li>
</ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->
]]></content:encoded>
    <excerpt:encoded><![CDATA[Global health practitioner at UNFPA Bangladesh — maternal &amp; reproductive health, MPDSR, SRH in humanitarian emergencies.]]></excerpt:encoded>
