  <!-- POST 1: Travel Blog -->
  <item>
    <title>Her Health, Her Right: Ending Obstetric Fistula in Hard-to-Reach Bangladesh</title>
    <link>https://animeshbiswas.com/2025/03/15/her-health-her-right/</link>
    <pubDate>Sat, 15 Mar 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
    <dc:creator><![CDATA[animesh]]></dc:creator>
    <guid isPermaLink="false">https://animeshbiswas.com/?p=101</guid>
    <description></description>
    <content:encoded><![CDATA[
<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><em>The invisible suffering of women like Sabika Moni — and what structural change it will take to end preventable fistula in the country's most underserved communities.</em></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Obstetric fistula remains one of the most devastating and least visible maternal health injuries in the world. Behind the clinical name is a woman — often young, often poor, often in a place a clinic has never quite reached.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>The structural causes</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The conditions that produce fistula are rarely about a single failed delivery. They are about the long chain of decisions before it: whether she could finish school, whether the road to the nearest facility was passable, whether the facility had a trained provider on the night her labor stalled.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2>What the field has taught us</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Over a decade of working in hard-to-reach areas of Bangladesh, three things have become clear:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list {"ordered":true} -->
<ol>
  <li><strong>Surveillance precedes response.</strong> You cannot fix what you do not count.</li>
  <li><strong>Community trust is infrastructure.</strong> It is built slowly and lost quickly.</li>
  <li><strong>Cash, where appropriate, dignifies care.</strong> Vouchers and direct transfers can do what clinics alone cannot.</li>
</ol>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><em>This is placeholder text. Replace with the full essay in WordPress.</em></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->
]]></content:encoded>
    <excerpt:encoded><![CDATA[The invisible suffering of women like Sabika Moni — and what structural change it will take to end preventable fistula in the country's most underserved communities.]]></excerpt:encoded>
    <wp:post_id>101</wp:post_id>
