  <!-- POST 3: Travel Blog -->
  <item>
    <title>Why Every Maternal Death Must Be Counted, Reviewed, and Acted Upon</title>
    <link>https://animeshbiswas.com/2024/11/10/why-every-maternal-death/</link>
    <pubDate>Sun, 10 Nov 2024 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
    <dc:creator><![CDATA[animesh]]></dc:creator>
    <guid isPermaLink="false">https://animeshbiswas.com/?p=103</guid>
    <description></description>
    <content:encoded><![CDATA[
<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><em>The case for institutionalising death surveillance systems at national scale — and the political will, community trust and patience that this kind of system genuinely demands.</em></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Maternal Perinatal Death Surveillance and Response (MPDSR) is, at its core, a moral commitment dressed in technical language: every death deserves a name, a review, and a response.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->
]]></content:encoded>
    <excerpt:encoded><![CDATA[The case for institutionalising death surveillance systems at national scale — and the political will, community trust and patience that this kind of system genuinely demands.]]></excerpt:encoded>
