  <!-- POST 4: Travel Blog -->
  <item>
    <title>What the Rohingya Response Taught Us About SRH at Scale</title>
    <link>https://animeshbiswas.com/2024/10/05/rohingya-srh-at-scale/</link>
    <pubDate>Sat, 05 Oct 2024 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
    <dc:creator><![CDATA[animesh]]></dc:creator>
    <guid isPermaLink="false">https://animeshbiswas.com/?p=104</guid>
    <description></description>
    <content:encoded><![CDATA[
<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><em>Five years of operational lessons from one of the largest humanitarian responses of the decade — what travelled, what didn't, and what the field is still learning.</em></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The Rohingya response was not a single emergency. It was a sequence of emergencies inside an emergency, each requiring SRH to be re-designed for the next phase of a population that was, by then, no longer transient.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->
]]></content:encoded>
    <excerpt:encoded><![CDATA[Five years of operational lessons from one of the largest humanitarian responses of the decade.]]></excerpt:encoded>
